2. In these Regulations —
“authorised representative”, in relation to a partnership (other than a limited liability partnership), means any person authorised to accept service of documents on behalf of the partnership;
“business address” means —
(a)in the case of an individual — the individual’s usual or last known place of business in Singapore; or
(b)in the case of a partnership (other than a limited liability partnership) — the partnership’s principal or last known place of business in Singapore;
“chosen means of access”, in relation to a person (X) on whom is or is to be served a document, means an electronic means agreed upon between X and another person serving the document as the means by which X may access that document’s contents;
“chosen means of notification”, in relation to a person (X) on whom is or is to be served a document, means an electronic means nominated by X to another person serving the document as the means by which X may be notified that such a document has been served on X;
“document” includes a notice or an order;
“last email address”, in relation to a person (X) on whom is or is to be served a document, means the last email address given by X to another person serving the document as the email address for the service of documents under the Act;
“residential address”, in relation to an individual, means the place of residence of an individual as registered under the National Registration Act 1965;
“serve”, in relation to a document, includes to give or send the document to a person.

4. A document to be served on an individual (X) may be served —
(a)by giving it to X personally;
(b)by sending it by registered post to —
(i)the address specified by X for the service of documents generally, or specifically for the document; or
(ii)if no address is so specified — X’s residential address or business address;
(c)by leaving it at X’s residential address with an adult apparently resident there, or at X’s business address with an adult apparently employed there;
(d)by affixing a copy of the document in a conspicuous place at X’s residential address or business address; or
(e)by sending it by fax to the fax number last known to the person serving the document as the fax number for the service of documents on X.

8. Service of a document takes effect —
(a)if the document is sent by registered post — 2 days after the date on which the document was posted (even if it is returned undelivered);
(b)if the document is sent by fax and a notification of successful transmission is received — on the day of transmission;
(c)if the document is sent by email — at the time that the email becomes capable of being retrieved by the person to whom it is sent;
(d)if the document is posted on a website mentioned in regulation 7(1)(c)(i) — at the beginning of the day after the date on which the document was posted; or
(e)if the document is sent to an account on social media mentioned in regulation 7(1)(c)(ii) — at the beginning of the day after the date on which the document was sent.
